# Events on the road (data/random_encounters/svalich_road.json and svalich_woods.json). Each plays on the table's
# road map once; when it ends without a fight the journey goes on. Fights come from the map's own encounters:
# road_dead_procession (road_ambush) and road_hunters (road_forest).

# --- Strahd rides past (rare, either road; never a fight) ---

~ strahd_rides
if flag.strahd_road_encounter
-> END
endif
cutscene strahd_rides
Narrator: Hoofbeats, unhurried, out of the fog ahead. A black horse with eyes like banked coals comes down the road at a walk, and the man riding it does not need to be introduced.
if flag.strahd_met
if flag.strahd_first_impression == "defiant"
Strahd [smile]: My guests, on my road. The ones who told me no across a graveside. I have thought about it often. It was refreshing.
elif flag.strahd_first_impression == "courteous"
Strahd: My guests, on my road, and still so well mannered. I did hope the village would not cure you of it.
elif flag.strahd_first_impression == "violent"
Strahd [smile]: Ah. The ones who drew steel at a funeral. I keep the memory the way one keeps a pressed flower.
else
Strahd: My quiet guests. You said nothing at the graveside. Let us see whether the road has loosened your tongues.
endif
else
Strahd: Good evening. You will be the guests my wolves keep telling me about. I am Strahd von Zarovich. This is my road. I do hope you are enjoying it.
endif
set strahd_met
if guest:ireena
Strahd: Ireena. The road suits you; the cold puts colour in your face. Are they treating you well?
Ireena [angry]: Better than you would.
Strahd [smile]: That is not a high bar, I grant you. I am working on it.
endif
if tarokka.drawn
Strahd: You have been to see the old woman at the pool. She always did love an audience. Did she tell you where to dig?
endif
if flag.doru_freed
Strahd: And my thanks for the boy from under the church. He arrived hungry and grateful. Such a rare combination.
endif
if flag.tser_pool_brawl_won
Strahd: You quarrelled with the Vistani. A pity. They are so useful, and so easily frightened.
endif
-> strahd_menu

~ strahd_menu
* Tell him to get off the road. -> s_defiant
* Return his courtesy. -> s_courteous
* [if guest:ireena] Step between him and Ireena. -> s_shield
* Draw on him. -> s_violent
* Say nothing. -> s_silent

~ s_defiant
set strahd_road_encounter = "defiant"
Strahd [smile]: Off my road. In my land. Under my sky. You have a gift for comedy. Good evening.
Narrator: He rides on through the middle of you. The black horse never breaks its walk, and you find you have stepped aside without meaning to.
approve thistle +2 godrick_pendlebrook +1 kip_smudgewick -1: You told Strahd to get off the road
-> END

~ s_courteous
set strahd_road_encounter = "courteous"
Strahd: There. You see? Civilisation survives, even here. We will dine together, one evening. I insist.
Narrator: He touches two fingers to his brow and rides on into the fog, and the fog closes behind him like a curtain.
approve liriel_dawnsong +1 kip_smudgewick +1 thistle -1 wren_featherfoot -1: You returned Strahd's courtesy on the road
-> END

~ s_shield
set strahd_road_encounter = "shield"
Strahd: How gallant. She hardly needs you there; she can refuse me perfectly well on her own. She has been doing it for centuries.
Ireena: What does that mean?
Strahd [smile]: Ask the old woman at the pool. Or ask me, over dinner. Good evening, Ireena.
approve godrick_pendlebrook +3 liriel_dawnsong +1 thistle +1 wren_featherfoot +1: You stepped between Strahd and Ireena
-> END

~ s_violent
set strahd_road_encounter = "violent"
Narrator: Steel clears leather. The black horse doesn't flinch. Your blow passes through the place where he was and closes on cold fog that smells of old roses.
Strahd: Not on the road. The road is for travelling. We will do this properly, in my house, when you are ready. You are not ready.
Narrator: His laughter comes from behind you, then from far away, then not at all.
approve thistle +1 kip_smudgewick -2 ratatoille -1: You drew on Strahd on the open road
-> END

~ s_silent
set strahd_road_encounter = "silent"
Strahd: Silence. How restful. Keep it; I have a great deal of my own.
Narrator: He rides on. Long after the hoofbeats fade, nobody wants to be the first to speak.
-> END

# --- A funeral on the road (day, Old Svalich Road) ---

~ funeral
if flag.funeral_met
-> END
endif
set funeral_met
Narrator: Up the road comes a handcart with a plain coffin on it, pushed by a stooped farmer and pulled by a boy of ten. Neither looks up until they are close enough to touch.
Bogdan: Morning. Or what passes for it. My mother, in the box. We're taking her to the church in the village. I won't put her in the ground unblessed, not with things the way they are.
if flag.donavich_refused_rites or flag.doru_freed
Bogdan: They say the priest won't open his doors any more. We'll knock anyway. What else is there?
elif flag.burgomaster_buried
Bogdan: Heard the burgomaster went into the ground proper, at last. Good. Then somebody still remembers how.
endif
if guest:ireena
Bogdan: Lady Ireena? Out here? My condolences, lady. Your father dug our well with his own hands, once. Wouldn't take a copper for it.
Ireena [sad]: That sounds like him.
endif
-> funeral_menu

~ funeral_menu
* [if not flag.anca_examined] [Medicine DC 13] Look at the old woman before they go on. -> anca_marks | anca_nothing
* [if not flag.anca_examined] [Cleric] Bless her, here on the road. -> anca_bless
* Give them something for the priest. -> anca_coin
* Wish them a safe road. -> anca_goodbye

~ anca_nothing
set anca_examined
Narrator: An old woman, grey and peaceful, with her hands folded on a sprig of dry thyme. Whatever took her, it left her looking asleep.
-> funeral_menu

~ anca_bless
set anca_examined
Narrator: You lay a hand on the coffin and begin the words. Cold comes up through the wood into your palm. Then you see the marks.
inspire class:cleric: blessed a dead stranger's coffin on the road
-> anca_marks

~ anca_marks
set anca_examined
Narrator: Two small punctures at her throat, under the collar, as neat as a seamstress's work. She did not die of age. She died of visits.
* Tell Bogdan what you've found. -> anca_tell
* Say nothing. Let them go. -> anca_silent

~ anca_tell
Bogdan [afraid]: She said a gentleman came to the window. Said he was lonely. She was always kind to the lonely. Oh, Mother.
* [Religion DC 12] Tell him what has to be done before she wakes. -> anca_stake | anca_hurry
* Tell him to get her to the church, fast. -> anca_hurry

~ anca_stake
set anca_fate = "staked"
Narrator: Bogdan sends the boy to sit by the cart with his back turned. It is quick. It is not easy. Afterwards he closes the lid himself and stands with his hand on it.
Bogdan [sad]: Thank you. I won't say it again, so hear it now. Thank you.
interject class:cleric: She'll sleep now. Properly, this time.
approve liriel_dawnsong +2 godrick_pendlebrook +1: You helped Bogdan see his mother properly to rest
-> END

~ anca_hurry
set anca_fate = "warned"
Bogdan [afraid]: The church. Before dark. Come on, Petru, pull, pull!
Narrator: The cart goes away toward the village at a speed no coffin was built for.
-> END

~ anca_silent
set anca_fate = "unwarned"
Narrator: They go on toward the village, the cart creaking, the boy pulling. The old woman's hands are folded very neatly. Nobody in this valley would think to look at her throat.
approve liriel_dawnsong -2 godrick_pendlebrook -2 kip_smudgewick -1: You let Bogdan carry his mother home without warning him what she'll become
-> END

~ anca_coin
gold -5
Bogdan: That's... thank you. That's a priest's fee and a candle besides. Mother would have made you take soup for it.
approve kip_smudgewick +1 godrick_pendlebrook +1: You paid a stranger's priest fee on the road
-> funeral_menu

~ anca_goodbye
if not flag.anca_fate
set anca_fate = "unknown"
endif
Bogdan: And to you. Keep off the road after dark. Everybody knows that, but people forget.
-> END

# --- The dead walking in procession (night, Old Svalich Road) ---

~ dead_procession
if flag.dead_procession_met
-> END
endif
set dead_procession_met
cutscene dead_procession
Narrator: Lanterns on the road ahead, swaying in a line: a funeral procession, out at the one hour no living Barovian would walk. Mourners in grey carry an open coffin between them. It is empty.
Narrator: As they come close, the one at the front lifts his lantern to your faces, one after another, as if measuring.
interject tag:blunt: Six of them. None of them breathing.
* [Stealth DC 13] Get off the road and into the ditch, quietly. -> dp_hidden | dp_seen
* [Cleric] [Religion DC 14] Raise your holy symbol and send them back to their graves. -> dp_turned | dp_fight
* Stand and fight. -> dp_fight

~ dp_hidden
Narrator: They pass so close you could touch the coffin. The one at the front stops beside your ditch, lifts his face, breathes in where breathing does no good, and walks on.
-> END

~ dp_seen
Narrator: The lantern swings toward the ditch and stops. The lead mourner says three words, in a voice like a door that has not been opened in years: room for one.
combat road_dead_procession

~ dp_turned
set dead_procession_turned
Narrator: The light of your faith hits them like a wind. They set the empty coffin down in the middle of the road, turn together, and walk off into the fields toward wherever they were buried.
interject tag:cheerful: We're just going to leave the coffin there? In the road? All right.
inspire class:cleric: turned a dead procession back to their graves
-> END

~ dp_fight
combat road_dead_procession

# --- A raven that walks beside you (day, either road) ---

~ ravens
if flag.ravens_met
-> END
endif
set ravens_met
Narrator: A raven drops onto the road a few paces ahead and walks beside you, the way a dog would, for the better part of a mile. When you stop, it stops. When you look at it, it looks back.
-> ravens_menu

~ ravens_menu
* [if not flag.raven_studied] [Nature DC 12] Watch it closely. -> raven_study_ok | raven_study_fail
* [if item:ration] Toss it a bit of food. -> raven_feed
* Shoo it away. -> raven_shoo
* Bring it down. It might be his. -> raven_harm

~ raven_study_ok
set raven_studied
Narrator: Its eyes follow conversations, not movements. When someone says the name of the lord on the hill, every feather on it lifts at once. Whatever this bird is, it is not his.
-> ravens_menu

~ raven_study_fail
set raven_studied
Narrator: A big black bird with a big black beak, and opinions. Beyond that it keeps its own counsel.
-> ravens_menu

~ raven_feed
take ration 1
set raven_fed
Narrator: It takes the crust, considers it, and then, quite unmistakably, nods. It flies off west toward the vineyards beyond Vallaki, and circles back twice to make sure you saw which way.
approve thistle +2 kip_smudgewick +1: You fed a raven on the road
-> END

~ raven_shoo
Narrator: It hops out of reach, plainly offended, and flies off west.
-> END

~ raven_harm
set raven_harmed
Narrator: It tumbles into the ditch, struggles up and flies away low and lopsided, shrieking. From the trees on both sides of the road, a great many ravens shriek back.
approve thistle -2 liriel_dawnsong -1 wren_featherfoot -1: You brought a raven down for no good reason
-> END

# --- Wolf hunters in the woods (day, Svalich Woods) ---

~ hunters
if flag.hunters_met
-> END
endif
set hunters_met
Narrator: A bowstring creaks in the trees to the left, and another to the right. A grizzled man steps onto the road ahead with an arrow on the string, not quite aimed at anybody.
Grigor: That's close enough. Strangers on this road, this near dark, are mostly his. Give me a reason to think you're not.
if guest:ireena
Narrator: His eyes go to Ireena, and the bow drops an inch.
Grigor: Kolyan's girl? Out here? Then the world's ended and nobody told me.
-> hunters_friends
endif
-> hunters_menu

~ hunters_menu
* [Persuasion DC 13] We're travellers, and we've been killing his wolves. -> h_talk_ok | h_talk_fail
* [if not flag.hunters_read] [Insight DC 12] Read him. -> h_read | h_read_fail
* [Intimidation DC 14] Lower the bow, or we'll lower it for you. -> h_scared | h_fight
* Attack first. -> h_fight

~ h_read
set hunters_read
Narrator: His hands are steady, but he hasn't blinked in a while. Three young men in the trees, all his kin by their noses. They are more afraid of you than you are of them, which makes them dangerous.
-> hunters_menu

~ h_read_fail
set hunters_read
Narrator: A hard man with a bow, and friends in the trees. That much was already clear.
-> hunters_menu

~ h_talk_ok
-> hunters_friends

~ h_talk_fail
Grigor: That's what his things say too. Walk past, slow, hands where I can see them.
Narrator: You walk past slowly. The arrows follow you all the way to the bend in the road.
-> END

~ h_scared
Narrator: He lowers the bow. In the trees, the other bows lower too, one by one.
Grigor: Fine. Go on, then. And may the wolves find you before you find us again.
-> END

~ h_fight
combat road_hunters

~ hunters_friends
set hunters_befriended
Narrator: The bow comes down. A whistle, and three young men drop out of the trees, all with the same nose.
Grigor: The wolves took my brother off this road a month back. We've been taking them back since, one pelt at a time.
Grigor: Two things, for free. There's an old windmill on a crag on the way to Vallaki. Don't knock. Crows on the sails, and some nights a child crying inside, and nobody in this valley has a child to spare.
set bonegrinder_rumor
Grigor: And the big wolves, the ones that walk on two legs when it suits them, den in the hills above the lake. They pray to some mother of theirs. Keep clear.
set werewolf_rumor
-> END

# --- A lost pack in the ditch (day, either road) ---

~ lost_bundle
if flag.lost_bundle_found
-> END
endif
set lost_bundle_found
Narrator: In the ditch beside the road lies a peddler's pack with its straps torn through. No peddler. A long smear in the mud leads off into the trees, and stops.
-> lost_bundle_menu

~ lost_bundle_menu
* Take what's useful. -> lb_take
* [if not flag.lost_bundle_tracked] [Survival DC 13] Follow the drag marks a little way. -> lb_track_ok | lb_track_fail
* Leave it. It's somebody's. -> lb_leave

~ lb_take
give ration 2
give torch 2
gold +4
Narrator: Rations, torches, four gold pieces knotted in a sock. And a letter, half written, that begins: the road is safer than they say, my love, and stops there.
approve kip_smudgewick -1 godrick_pendlebrook -1: You went through a lost traveller's bundle and took what was useful
-> END

~ lb_track_ok
set lost_bundle_tracked
set werewolf_rumor
Narrator: Fifty paces in, the marks end at a pine scored with claw marks higher than a tall man can reach. Whatever took the peddler stood up on two legs to do it.
-> lost_bundle_menu

~ lb_track_fail
set lost_bundle_tracked
Narrator: The marks lose themselves in pine needles. The woods are very quiet, in the way that means something is listening.
-> lost_bundle_menu

~ lb_leave
Narrator: You leave it for whoever comes looking. You suspect nobody will.
approve kip_smudgewick +1 godrick_pendlebrook +1: You left a lost traveller's bundle for whoever comes looking
-> END
